'My approach is to use the YOLOv8 segmentation model, which is well-suited for instance segmentation tasks. I will first convert the provided `train_dataset` and `val_dataset` into the YOLO format using the built-in `generate_yolo_dataset` method. Then, I will train a `yolov8s-seg` model on this data for 50 epochs with an image size of 1024 to avoid losing detail from downsampling. After training, I will load the best-performing model weights and perform inference on each image in the validation set. Finally, I will process the model's output masks, assigning a unique integer ID to each detected cell instance and combining them into a single `uint16` mask per image as required.'
