'My approach is to use the YOLOv8m-seg model, a strong baseline for instance segmentation. I will first convert the provided datasets into YOLO format using the helper function and then train the model for 50 epochs on high-resolution 1024x1024 images to capture fine cellular details, with early stopping (patience=15) to prevent overfitting and optimize training time. After training, I will load the best-performing model checkpoint to run inference on the validation images. For the final output, I will post-process the raw predictions by sorting detected instances by their confidence scores to resolve any overlaps and then assign a unique `uint16` ID to each cell, constructing the required instance masks. As an evaluation metric, I will calculate and print the average Jaccard index across the validation set.'
