'The previous solution utilized a `yolov8s-seg` model, which lacks the capacity for this complex segmentation task and consistently underfits the data. My proposed improvement is to increase the model's capacity by switching to the larger and more powerful `yolov8m-seg` model, which is better suited to learn the intricate features in high-resolution cell microscopy images. To accommodate the larger model's memory requirements, I will reduce the batch size to 2. Additionally, I will correct a critical bug in the post-processing logic to ensure that when predicted masks overlap, the one with the higher confidence score correctly takes precedence in the final instance mask.'
