'The previous solution utilized a `yolov8s-seg` model, which, given the complexity and high resolution of microscopy images, may lack the capacity to learn the fine-grained features necessary for accurate cell segmentation, leading to underfitting. My proposed improvement is to increase the model's capacity by replacing it with the larger `yolov8m-seg` model. This more powerful architecture should be better equipped to capture the intricate details of the cells, and to manage its higher memory requirements, I will reduce the training batch size from 4 to 2. Additionally, I will correct a critical bug in the post-processing logic to ensure that when predicted masks overlap, the one with the higher confidence score correctly takes precedence.'
