'The previous solution utilized a `yolov8s-seg` model, which, given the complexity and high resolution of microscopy images, may lack the capacity to learn the fine-grained features necessary for accurate cell segmentation, leading to underfitting. To address this, my proposed improvement is to increase the model's capacity by replacing it with the larger `yolov8m-seg` model. This more powerful architecture should be better equipped to capture the intricate details of the cells. To accommodate the larger model's memory requirements on the available hardware and ensure stable training, I will also reduce the batch size from 4 to 2.'
