'The previous solution utilized a `yolov8s-seg` model which has insufficient capacity for this complex segmentation task, leading to underfitting, and it also contained a critical bug where lower-confidence masks would incorrectly overwrite higher-confidence ones. My proposed improvement is to increase the model's capacity by switching to the larger `yolov8m-seg` model to better learn intricate cell features. To manage the increased memory and computational load of the larger model and prevent timeouts, I will reduce the training epochs from 50 to 25 and the batch size from 4 to 2. Finally, I will correct the post-processing logic to ensure that when predicted masks overlap, the one with the higher confidence score correctly takes precedence.'
