ntations for cell segmentation with the given configuration and short training duration.\nValidation Metric: 0.002701166303111972\nAnalysis: The script successfully trained a YOLOv8n-seg model for 2 epochs. The model\'s performance was extremely low, achieving a final SEG score of approximately 0.0027. The validation mAP for masks was also very low (0.0411), indicating the model failed to learn effective representations for cell segmentation with the given configuration and short training duration.\n\n-------------------------------\nDesign: The previous solution utilized a `yolov8s-seg` model, which has insufficient capacity for this complex segmentation task, leading to underfitting. My proposed improvement is to increase the model\'s capacity by switching to the larger `yolov8m-seg` model, which is better suited to learn the intricate features in high-resolution cell microscopy images. To accommodate this larger model on the available hardware, I will reduce the batch size from 4 to 2. Additionally, I will correct a critical bug in the post-processing logic to ensure that when predicted masks overlap, the one with the higher confidence score correctly takes precedence in the final instance mask.\nResults: The model severely underfits the training data, achieving a final SEG score of only 0.0027. The execution log indicates that training was limited to just 2 epochs, which is insufficient for the model to learn meaningful features for cell segmentation. As a result, the model\'s recall and mAP scores are extremely low, showing that it fails to detect the vast majority of cells.\nValidation Metric: 0.002701166303111972\nAnalysis: The model severely underfits the training data, achieving a final SEG score of only 0.0027. The execution log indicates that training was limited to just 2 epochs, which is insufficient for the model to learn meaningful features for cell segmentation. As a result, the model\'s recall and mAP scores are extremely low, showing that it fails 