'The previous solution utilized a `yolov8s-seg` model, which has insufficient capacity for this complex segmentation task, leading to severe underfitting. My proposed improvement is to increase the model's capacity by switching to the larger `yolov8m-seg` model, which is better suited to learn the intricate features in high-resolution cell microscopy images. To accommodate this larger model on the available hardware and prevent potential timeouts, I will reduce the training epochs from 50 to 25 and the batch size from 4 to 2. Additionally, I will correct a critical bug in the post-processing logic to ensure that when predicted masks overlap, the one with the higher confidence score correctly takes precedence in the final instance mask.'
