'The previous solution contains a critical bug in its post-processing logic where lower-confidence instance masks can incorrectly overwrite higher-confidence ones in overlapping areas. My primary improvement is to correct this by modifying the mask assembly loop to ensure that a pixel is assigned to a new instance ID only if it has not already been assigned to a higher-confidence instance from a previous iteration. This guarantees that in areas of overlap, the prediction with the highest confidence score takes precedence. To ensure the training process completes within the strict time limit and avoids the fallback to a minimal 2-epoch run, I will also reduce the total number of training epochs from 50 to a more conservative 15, striking a balance between model convergence and execution time.'
