'The previous solution contains a critical bug in its post-processing logic where lower-confidence instance masks can incorrectly overwrite higher-confidence ones in overlapping areas. My primary improvement is to correct this by modifying the mask assembly loop to ensure a pixel is only assigned to a new instance if it hasn't already been claimed by a higher-confidence prediction. To also ensure the training process completes successfully within the strict time limit and avoids the fallback to a minimal 2-epoch run, I will reduce the total training epochs from 50 to a more conservative 15. This dual change ensures both correct mask generation and that a reasonably trained model is produced.'
