'The previous solution contains a critical bug in its post-processing logic where lower-confidence instance masks can incorrectly overwrite higher-confidence ones in overlapping areas. My primary improvement is to correct this by modifying the mask assembly loop to ensure a pixel is only assigned to a new instance if it has not already been claimed by a higher-confidence prediction. This guarantees that in areas of overlap, the prediction with the highest confidence score correctly takes precedence. To ensure the training process completes successfully within the strict time limit and avoids the fallback to a minimal 2-epoch run, I will also reduce the total training epochs from 50 to a more conservative 12.'
